      "text": "To determine the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we start by finding the prime factorizations of both numbers.\n\nFirst, let's factorize 342:\n\\[ 342 \\div 2 = 171 \\]\n\\[ 171 \\div 3 = 57 \\]\n\\[ 57 \\div 3 = 19 \\]\n\\[ 19 \\div 19 = 1 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n\\[ 342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19 \\]\n\nNext, let's factorize 285:\n\\[ 285 \\div 3 = 95 \\]\n\\[ 95 \\div 5 = 19 \\]\n\\[ 19 \\div 19 = 1 \\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n\\[ 285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19 \\]\n\nNow, we identify the common factors of 342 and 285. The common factors are the prime factors that appear in both factorizations. The only common prime factor is 19. Therefore, the greatest common divisor (gcd) of 342 and 285 is:\n\\[ \\gcd(342, 285) = 19 \\]\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{19} \\]",
